6-bit EXL3 decodeGroup for stitched Flash Next projections (in_proj_qkv+z, q+k+v)

Extends TensorFold's EXL3 projection-group kernel (`tf_exl3_group`) from 4-bit
(`halves == 8`) to 6-bit `mul1` (`halves == 12`, `tf_exl3_group_12_2_{4,8}`),
and batches stitched 6-bit decode projections in `cuda_exl3_lane.zig` into one
Hadamard rotation + one GEMM launch (gated by `TF_EXL3_DECODE_GROUP`, default 1).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2):
- 1-stream decode: +2.3% to +3.4% (code 106.6 -> 109.0, prose 52.2 -> 54.0, json 101.8 -> 104.4 tok/s)
- 4-stream decode: +1.5% prose (107.0 -> 108.6 steady), +0.5% json
- Exactness: 5/5 greedy and 5/5 T=0.7 token_sha256 identical to stock, drafts on == drafts off.

